re gas and  flow rate within the microfluidics plate  which is connected to the controller by  manifold  the software is very easy to use and  enables step-by-step protocol building  where each experimental step can be  built with user defined time temperature  gas and perfusion parameter such as flow  rate  let's take a look at the plate  in greater details  it has standard 96 well footprint  image in the centers show  one of our plate pre-loaded with colored  dyes to show individual layout of the  fluidics  plate has a six inlet oils on the left  side and two outlet wells on the right  side  connected to the central tissue culture  chamber area via microfluidics channel  as you can see in this cartoon for each  row  indicators of group 1 2 3 and 4  all the individual well within the group  are connected to tissue culture chamber  area via individual micro fluids  channels which are the colored lines  this enables up to four independent  experiments to be conducted per plate  when the plane is connected to the  controller unit vr manifold  media or reagent in each of the inlet  wells can be pressed down via positive  pressure  this will then move the media or reagent  from that well into the tissue culture  chamber area  and which will then will exit to the  outer wells  essentially this creates a system where  any desired media or reagent can be  precisely delivered to cells in the  chamber area at desired time  for specific duration and with specific  flow rate  since the plate can be temperature and  gas control  we now have a system that can offer  ability to control cellular micro  environment in dynamic on demand fashion  plate material is also made of gas  permeable polymer to allow dynamic gas  control  and the bottom of the plate is made of n  1.5 glass for clear imaging including  confocal applications  last thing i would like to mention is  that since these are microfluidics plate  we can also introduce specific micro  dimensional features  targeting certain applications such as  imaging of suspension cells or  maintenance of chemotactic gradient  now let's go over some of the key  applications  our system can be connected to two  independent gas outlets  so in this example we can create  normoxic and hypoxic conditions using  gas switching ability  the middle image shows fluorescent  intensity of reverse oxygen sensor rtdp  measured from one of the tissue culture  chamber within our microfluidic plate  ittp will increase fluorescence with  decreasing oxygen concentration and vice  versa  arrows indicate the time point at which  gas switching was initiated  we can see rtdp fluorescence increasing  as we put tissue chamber under hypoxic  condition  starting at t equals two hours  when we revert to nomoxy condition  at t equals 6.5 hours we can see  fluorescence start to decrease  now that we have established that our  system can create hypoxic or nomostic  microenvironment the image on the right  shows cellular responses under such  conditions by measuring expression level  of heatphone alpha which is a key  transcription factor under cellular  hypoxia  we are also measuring itdp fluorescence  as indicated by blue line  when cells are subjected to hypoxic  condition  we see the expression level of heatphone  alpha increasing as seen by the increase  in the black line and then later on as  cells are subjected to the moxie  condition we see fluorescence of rtdp  decreasing which in turn is followed  rapidly by decreased expression of  hyphen alpha  intensity of dappy is plotted as a  control in purple line  and it shows no meaningful change under  changing oxygen levels  next we would like to show you lifestyle  movies generated using biotracker  hypoxia lifestyle dye this is a cell  permeable life cell dye  which becomes fluorescent under hypoxic  condition inside of cells  here we are looking at a431 cells  loaded with and without dye after 16  hour incubation under hypoxic condition  to show its specificity  now le